{"name":"Tart Gelato","hex":"#f6eec9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tart","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Sharp to the taste; acid; sour.","High or too high in acidity."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of small open pie, or piece of pastry, now typically containing jelly (US) / jam (UK) or conserve, or sometimes other fillings (chocolate, custard, egg, butter, historically even meat or other savory fillings).","A melt (block of wax for use in a tart burner)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tart"},{"term":"gelato","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An Italian variant of ice cream made from milk and sugar, combined with other flavourings. The ingredients are supercooled while stirring to break up ice crystals as they form."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gelato"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tart","blocks":[{"text":"A tart is a baked dish consisting of a filling over a pastry base with an open top not covered with pastry. The pastry is usually shortcrust pastry; the filling may be sweet or savoury, though modern tarts are usually fruit-based, sometimes with custard. Tartlet refers to a miniature tart; an example would be egg tarts. The categories of \"tart\", \"flan\", and \"pie\" overlap, with no sharp distinctions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Raspberry_tart.jpg/330px-Raspberry_tart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tart","wikidata":"Q1142483"},{"title":"Gelato","blocks":[{"text":"Gelato refers to a specific type of ice cream of Italian origin. In Italian, gelato is the common word for all types of ice cream. Artisanal gelato in Italy generally contains 6–9% butterfat, which is lower than other styles of frozen dessert. Gelato typically contains 20–35% air, and more flavoring than other types of frozen desserts, giving it an intense flavor with creamy, smooth texture, density and richness that distinguishes it from other ice creams."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Delicious_Gelato_on_display.jpg/330px-Delicious_Gelato_on_display.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gelato","wikidata":"Q1362405"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Akashi_City_Museum_of_Culture_Hyogo_pref_Japan13s.jpg/500px-Akashi_City_Museum_of_Culture_Hyogo_pref_Japan13s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Akashi_City_Museum_of_Culture_Hyogo_pref_Japan13s.jpg/1280px-Akashi_City_Museum_of_Culture_Hyogo_pref_Japan13s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Akashi_City_Museum_of_Culture_Hyogo_pref_Japan13s.jpg/500px-Akashi_City_Museum_of_Culture_Hyogo_pref_Japan13s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Piece of apple tart","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAkashi_City_Museum_of_Culture_Hyogo_pref_Japan13s.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/00_Lemon_Meringue_Tarts.jpg/500px-00_Lemon_Meringue_Tarts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/00_Lemon_Meringue_Tarts.jpg/1280px-00_Lemon_Meringue_Tarts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/00_Lemon_Meringue_Tarts.jpg/500px-00_Lemon_Meringue_Tarts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lemon meringue tarts","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A00_Lemon_Meringue_Tarts.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/